From 9cf28bfe735048befcb84ce495329db939cdebad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 21:24:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Run healthy and edema kernels back to back, 60 degrees only

Both kernels now simulate in one run rather than being selected by a preset.
Steps 3 to 8 are wrapped in for ik = 1:NKERN, so the two share the same
ground truth, protocol and noise seeds and differ only in the kernel; each
iteration stashes into RUN{ik} and the figures read from there. The single
fibre condition is dropped -- ANGLES is now 60 alone, and the general
walkthrough still covers single fibres.

That means Steps 3 to 8 cannot be run as isolated Live Script cells any
more, since they are inside a loop. The section that opens the loop says so.

The figures are rebuilt around the pair:

  1  the ground truth fODF, then each kernel's response glyph per shell.
     The old Figure 1 was a single kernel-independent glyph once the single
     fibre went, so it is folded in here as the left column -- what is being
     convolved, beside what it is convolved with
  2  the spherical signal, healthy: b down the rows, SNR across
  3  the same for edema, on ONE shared radial scale computed across both
     kernels, so the two compare by eye and not only by number
  4  reconstructed fODFs, healthy: Lmax down, truth then one column per SNR
  5  the same for edema
  6  bias, spread and spurious peaks against SNR, ONE ROW PER KERNEL, with y
     limits shared per column so neither row is autoscaled to look like the
     other

A commented CSD / MSMT-CSD import sits just before Step 7, at the scoring
stage rather than the figure stage. Uncommenting it makes them extra arms
scored by the SAME peak finder as SMI, so they become extra columns in
Figures 4 and 5 and extra curves in Figure 6 with no change to figure code.
It records the two things that have bitten this package before: dwi2fod
needs -lmax matching LMAX_LIST or the ceiling is the wrong bound, and an
MRtrix FOD is not normalised while an SMI fODF integrates to 1, so any
shared radial scale has to normalise first.

Runtime doubles to 36 fits, offset by halving the voxels per fit now that
the single fibre condition is gone.

No simulation was run. The six-figure block was executed against the
repository's graphics stubs with fabricated RUN data, which exercises the
indexing, the glyph calls, the SH fits and the summary plots; only the
drawing itself is untested, as in every notebook here.

